  "source": "unsafe base.\nBench.start : Unit -> Unit .\nBench.elapsed : Unit -> Int .\n# bench: small helper functions called in a hot loop (the shape most library\n# and application code has): clamp, lerp, a mix built from both, and a\n# higher-order helper given a known function\nclamp : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int .\nclamp lo hi x = if x < lo then lo else if x > hi then hi else x.\nlerp : Int -> Int -> Int -> Int .\nlerp a b t = a + (b - a) * t / 256.\nmix : Int -> Int -> Int .\nmix x y = clamp 0 255 (lerp x y 77).\ntwice : (Int -> Int -> Int) -> Int -> Int -> Int .\ntwice f x y = f (f x y) y.\nloop : unsafe Int -> Int -> Int .\nloop n acc = if n == 0 then acc else loop (n - 1) (acc + twice mix (band n 255) (band acc 255)).\nmain = _ = Bench.start Unit; value = loop 10000000 0;\n  ns = Bench.elapsed Unit; print \"{value} {ns}\".\n",
